      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9414008::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "σ-phase precipitates normally form and grow during exposure at approximately 900–1300 K.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9414008::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC9414008::web::008::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At temperatures starting around 950 K, σ phase grows and preferentially occupies grain boundaries.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9414008::web::008::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "σ-phase precipitates act as local sites for accelerated oxidation or reduction reactions.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The presence and growth of σ phase can reduce mechanical and chemical properties.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9414008::web::008::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Localized degradation associated with σ phase causes embrittlement and premature or catastrophic failure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dissolving σ phase reduces localized degradation sites.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dissolving σ phase enhances overall mechanical stability during oxidizing or reducing gas exposure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Annealed samples will have lower degradation rates than as-manufactured samples, as indicated by mass change, hardness reduction, or crack initiation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Annealed samples will exhibit greater microstructural uniformity than the as-manufactured baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9414008::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Annealing will delay or prevent catastrophic failure during prolonged high-temperature gas exposure.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed governing behavior applies to oxidizing and reducing gas exposure at approximately 900–1300 K.",
